  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia, in partnership with the World Bank, supported analysis, research to drive legislative and policy changes. Key activities included:
&#x200d;
&#x2022;supporting the Mekong Delta Regional Master Plan, which guides regional climate-resilient and sustainable development and investment across 13 provinces.  
&#x200d;
&#x2022;Vietnam&#x2019;s first guidelines on career guidance and job counselling for students to improve access to labour market information helping them make informed career decisions. It is estimated 2.2 million students will benefit. 
&#x200d;
&#x2022;Drawing on e-payment pilot over the last two years, Australia supported guideline to all 63 provinces to rollout social assistance e-payment. Several provinces have adopted the guideline.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&#x2019;s partnership with the World Bank has &#x201c;strengthening policies and regulations&#x201d; as a key objective. The partnership supports improved governance of Vietnam by having more evidence-based for inclusive laws and policies development and decisions. To support implementation of the 2019 Labor Code, Australia&#x2019;s partnership with the World Bank supported research and studies for the Ministry of Labor, Invalids and Social Affairs (MOLISA) to develop a national implementation guideline which was officially launched in 2023. The guideline addressed gender equality barriers such as provision of childcare services and will be consistently applied by municipal officials for better planning and budgeting for childcare services.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate adaptation, mitigation, environment and biodiversity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&#x2019;s partnership with the World Bank in Vietnam (ABP2) supported increased resilience in the Mekong delta region through research and analysis to inform policies and programs to realize the Vietnam government&apos;s Mekong Regional Master Plan. ABP2 is also supporting Vietnam&#x2019;s ambition to achieve net zero by 2050 by helping to accelerate de-carbonization pathways in the power and transport sectors. ABP2&apos;s &#x201c;Recommendations to the National Roadmap and Action Plan for the Electric Mobility Transition&#x201d; were well received by the government of Vietnam. It contained recommendations to reduce carbon and methane emissions from the road transportation sector through transition to electric public transport.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved Governance</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&#x2019;s partnership with the World Bank in Vietnam (ABP2) supported the Government of Vietnam&#x2019;s policy change to address the lack of child-care services in industrial parks, a major barrier to woman&#x2019;s labour force participation.  ABP2&#x2019;s Urban Childcare Supply and Demand report directly informed the Vietnam Government&#x2019;s new &#x201c;National Scheme on Improving the Quality of Care and Education for Children of Factory Workers in Areas with Industrial Parks 2024-2030, with Vision to 2045&#x201d;.  When implemented, this scheme will provide subsidies to teachers and parents, incentives for public-private partnership schools, easier access to land and other quality assurance measures to improve quality childcare services in industrial parks.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate adaptation, mitigation, environment and biodiversity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&#x2019;s partnership with the World Bank is an investment that supports the Government of Vietnam (GOV) to strengthen development policies and programs in priority themes/sectors. The partnership has responded timely and effectively to Vietnam&#x2019;s, Australia&#x2019;s and the World Bank&#x2019;s priorities in combating climate change. Australia assisted Vietnam to strategically plan for actions and policies toward green growth and improve the economy resilience The partnership funded deep-dive studies on land suitability, water management, and climate risk assessment that helps Government Ministries and 13 provincial authorities to design future investment projects under the Mekong Delta Regional Master Plan which was approved by the GOV for implementation. Australia funded technical studies and assessments which contributed to development of Vietnam&#x2019;s Eighth Power Development Plan that has placed Vietnam on the net-zero emissions pathway by 2050 by calling for the doubling of renewable energy production and a 45 percent reduction in coal.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
